<title>SLOVAKIA: Slovakia posts Jan-Oct 96 c/a deficit of $1.17 bln.</title>
<headline>Slovakia posts Jan-Oct 96 c/a deficit of $1.17 bln.</headline>
<dateline>BRATISLAVA 1997-01-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Slovak current account recorded a deficit for the January-October period of $1.174 billion, compared with a $539.5 million surplus over the same period in 1995, the National Bank of Slovakia said on Thursday.</p>
<p>It added that the capital account was in surplus for the first ten months of 1996 by $1.252 billion, compared with a surplus of $167.4 million in the same period the previous year.  </p>
<p>  SLOVAK CURRENT ACCT   10MO'96   9MO'96   FY/95   10MO'95</p>
<p>  overall ($ million)     -1,174.1  -1,031.7  +648.8   +539.5</p>
<p>  trade balance	 -1,392.6  -1,221.6   +24.1    -55.6</p>
<p>  balance of services    +80.5     +79.0  +546.2   +523.5</p>
<p>  income balance	   -16.0     -23.2   -13.7     +1.5</p>
<p>  current transfers     +154.0    +134.1   +92.2    +70.1</p>
<p>CAPITAL ACCOUNT</p>
<p> Total balance		 +1,252.4 +1,202.9  +993.9 +167.4</p>
<p> capital transfers		+29.8    +29.9   +45.7  +45.7</p>
<p>direct investment balance</p>
<p>  inv. in Slovak republic    +108.3   +116.8  +141.9  +97.7</p>
<p>  Slovak investment abroad    -33.2    -18.2    -7.9   -8.0</p>
<p>portfolio investment balance</p>
<p>  inv. in Slovak Republic	+5.7     +6.7   +74.4   +7.2</p>
<p>  Slovak investment abroad    +68.3    +38.4  +171.7 +230.2</p>
<p>other long-term financial</p>
<p>  account			  +349.5   +385.5  +393.8  -65.7</p>
<p> short-term fin. account     +724.1  +643.7   +91.3   -96.7</p>
<p>Note. All figures are in millions of U.S. dollars. The</p>
<p>central bank used the following exchange rates in</p>
<p>calculating the figures: Jan-Oct '96 (USD=30.536 SKK),</p>
<p>Jan-Sept'96 (USD=30.427 SKK), full year '95 (USD=29.735</p>
<p>SKK), Jan-Oct '95 (USD=29.766).</p>
<p>-- Tatiana Vacova, Bratislava Newsroom, 42-7-536-3687</p>
